PDP-11 visitor counter — installed 2026-09-19

Display: VISITORS: n replaces THE MACHINE in the top masthead.
Count: approximate browser sessions since installation, not unique people.
One increment per browser-session cookie, with sessionStorage as fallback.
Reload navigation never increments. TOP refreshes never call the counter.
Cookies/session storage blocked: read only. No identity or IP list is stored.
Different browsers and hostnames can count separately. JavaScript is needed.
The session marker is reserved before the request to avoid double counting an
interrupted response. Failed first visits can therefore be missed. Simultaneous
first loads in different tabs may race. This is a lightweight visit estimate.

Paths:
  /usr/src/local/webtop/visit-counter.c  K&R, integer-only source
  /home/www/cgi-bin/visit               non-setuid, root-owned executable 755
  /home/www-visits/                     www-owned private directory, 700
  /home/www-visits/total                www-owned persistent count, 600
  /home/www-visits/lock                 www-owned stable flock file, 600
  /home/www-visits/total.new            temporary atomic replacement
  /home/www/visits.txt                  symlink to private total; httpd is www
  /usr/src/local/webtop/index.before-visitors.html  homepage backup

Build on 2.11BSD:
  cd /usr/src/local/webtop
  cc -O -o visit-counter visit-counter.c

Updates use flock, fsync, and rename. An eight-second alarm bounds the complete
CGI lifetime including lock waits and writes. Missing/corrupt/overflowed totals
return 503; they are never silently reset. The static total is fixed-width
(10 decimal digits + newline) to keep Content-Length stable during increments.
The display removes leading zeroes and uses thousands separators.

Back up /home/www-visits/total with the system. Do not reset it on redeployment.
Use a graceful shutdown for normal filesystem durability. This does not claim
a guarantee against arbitrary power loss or disk/filesystem damage.

The existing httpd, inetd, network settings, and TOP refresh rate are unchanged.
A caller can increment by requesting the CGI directly; this is not a fraud-
resistant analytics system. No ongoing counter polling or separate daemon.
